name walk_shoreline
describe Walk from inland ground down to the waterline, into the sea, swim, and climb back out. This is the scenario Prompt 001 Group A's swim/dive/shore-pop physics was hand-driven to check; it exercises all three Stances in one run, so a regression in any of them shows up as a ground violation or a stall rather than as a feeling.
backend both

option --walk

pose_ground 64,0 -90 -8 1.7
# Downhill along +X from 56 m to the waterline at about x=112, then into the sea and back out.
# The heights along this line, from tools/svo_render: 66.0, 56.2, 47.2, 13.5, -0.5 at x = 48..112.
#
# Goal 232 dropped walking from 10 m/s to 1.4, so the legs that have to COVER the 48 m to the
# waterline sprint (7 m/s); the leg that goes into the water walks, because entering the sea at a
# sprint is a different test from the one this scenario is named for and the swim physics are what
# it exists to exercise.
hold forward+boost 5
hold none 1
hold forward+boost 4
hold none 2
look 90 -5 1
hold forward 10

# A settle before the final capture. A moving scenario requests a whole-world rebuild every 2 m
# (run_svo's lod_radius*0.5), and whether the last one has LANDED by the final frame depends on
# wall-clock timing -- measured: fly_orbit's vk `final` differed from its own golden by 70.4% of
# pixels on a re-run while d3d12's was bit-identical, purely because one run's rebuild arrived
# and the other's did not. That is the rebuild storm Prompt 004 exists to remove; until it is
# removed, a golden taken immediately after motion is not reproducible. Waiting is the honest
# workaround, and this line should be deletable once 004 lands.
wait 3


# GOLDEN POLICY (measured, this scenario has none / only the early ones):
# A capture taken after sustained MOTION is not reproducible on this engine today. Two identical
# runs of the same scenario differ by 5.3% to 35.5% of pixels, because at speed the body outruns the
# LOD rebuild and which tree is resident when it stops decides what it sees. Captures taken AT REST
# reproduce to 0.0001-0.11%, well under the 1.5% gate. So the moving captures here are written for
# eyeballing and deliberately have no golden until Prompt 004 removes the rebuild storm.

capture event grounded on_ground no-golden
capture event world-ready first_light no-golden
capture end final no-golden
assert walk_violations == 0
assert inside_solid == 0
assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
